window.docContents[146].resolve({"/Elementary-Functions/___4___3-Graphics/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___3-Graphics--___4___3-Graphics--___4___3_LPAR_iii_RPAR_-Complex-Arguments___-Surfaces":{"contents":"Source: DLMF §4.3(iii).\n\nIn these graphics, height is the absolute value of the function and color is\nits phase.  The principal logarithm has a branch cut on the negative real axis.\n\n\\left|\\ln(x+\\mathrm{i}y)\\right|. The surface height is the modulus of the principal logarithm at x+i y; its\ncolor records the principal phase.  The displayed domain is the plane slit\nalong the nonpositive real axis, which makes the branch-cut discontinuity\nvisible.\n\n\\left|{\\mathrm e}^{x+\\mathrm{i}y}\\right|. For the exponential surface, the modulus depends only on the real coordinate:\n|exp(x+i y)| = exp x; the imaginary coordinate controls the phase and hence\nthe color bands.\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions\u0009§4.3 Graphics\u0009§4.3 Graphics","header":"§4.3(iii) Complex Arguments: Surfaces","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___3-Graphics/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Elementary-Functions--___4___3-Graphics--___4___3-Graphics--___4___3_LPAR_iii_RPAR_-Complex-Arguments___-Surfaces"},"/Elementary-Functions/___4___47-Approximations/#chapter-4-section-47":{"contents":"Source: NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, §4.47.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Elementary Functions","header":"4.47. §4.47 Approximations","id":"/Elementary-Functions/___4___47-Approximations/#chapter-4-section-47"},"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___12-Asymptotic-Expansions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___12-Asymptotic-Expansions--___6___12-Asymptotic-Expansions--Exponential-and-logarithmic-integrals":{"contents":"For E₁(z), the expansion holds for |ph z| ≤ 3π/2 − δ, with\n0 < δ < 3π/2, on the open principal-cut domain. This is the explicit\nopen-cut specialization of the principal-branch statement. The positive-real\nexpansion for Ei(x) uses the real part of the canonical §6.2 map realEi and\nis stated as x → +∞. The first-neglected-term estimates are recorded\nseparately: E₁ has a unit factor for |ph z| ≤ π/2 and a\ncsc(|ph z|) factor for π/2 ≤ |ph z| < π, with the same-sign property on\nthe positive axis. When the Ei expansion is retained through term index n,\nthe next term has index n+1 and the remainder bound has factor\n1 + χ(n+1), where χ is the Gamma quotient from §9.7.3.\n\nThe same-sign Lean companions use the explicit SameRealSign convention:\nboth quantities are real and their product is nonnegative. Thus “same sign” is\nread as “not opposite signs”; the totalized predicate also includes the case\nwhere one of the values is zero.\n\nE_{1}(z)\\sim e^{-z}z^{-1}\\sum_{k\\ge0}(-1)^k k!z^{-k}$$\n\n\n\n\n\nEi(x)\\sim e^x x^{-1}(1+1!x^{-1}+2!x^{-2}+\\cdots)$$\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Exponential, Logarithmic, Sine, and Cosine Integrals\u0009§6.12 Asymptotic Expansions\u0009§6.12 Asymptotic Expansions","header":"Exponential and logarithmic integrals","id":"/Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals/___6___12-Asymptotic-Expansions/#LMLF-___-DLMF-with-Lean--Exponential___-Logarithmic___-Sine___-and-Cosine-Integrals--___6___12-Asymptotic-Expansions--___6___12-Asymptotic-Expansions--Exponential-and-logarithmic-integrals"},"/Gamma-Function/Gamma-Function-___-___5___4-Special-Values-and-Extrema/#chapter-5-section-5-4":{"contents":"Source: NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, §5.4, Special Values and Extrema.\n\n\n\n","context":"LMLF · DLMF with Lean\u0009Gamma Function","header":"5.4. Gamma Function · §5.4 Special Values and Extrema","id":"/Gamma-Function/Gamma-Function-___-___5___4-Special-Values-and-Extrema/#chapter-5-section-5-4"}});